.DS_Store
.venv/
__pycache__/
screenshots/
.claude/

# Real Strava exports and anything built from them. An activity trace is a record of where
# someone lives and when they are not home, so it does not go in a public repo. Day 02's
# `fixture/` and the `data/` built from it are synthetic and ARE committed, so the window
# renders for someone without an export.
#
# `tools/prepare.py` writes to `private/` by default for this reason. Pointing its `--out` at
# `data/` publishes real traces; it prints its destination so that is a decision rather than
# an accident.
apps/day-*/private/
# Without a second pattern lacking the trailing slash, a *symlink* named `private` is not
# ignored — git treats the slash as "directory only" and a symlink is a blob. One got
# committed that way (92bc9fe, removed in the commit that added this line): a worktree needs
# the real data to run the day 02 checks, linking it in is the obvious way to get it, and the
# link sailed straight past the rule meant to stop exactly that.
apps/day-*/private
strava/
strava-export/
strava_export*/
export_*/
